  - m_Id: 25345767223844864
    m_Localized: Ik ga akkoord met de <b>Gebruiksvoorwaarden</b> en het <b>Privacybeleid</b>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25351728189661184
    m_Localized: Algemene voorwaarden
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25351921299611648
    m_Localized: "# Do you want to participate in the FOODMISSION Pilot Phase of
      FOODMISSION?\n\n**Purpose of the project**\n\nYou are invited to participate
      in a research project where the main purpose is to engage citizens as agents
      of change for sustainable food system transition. We aim to do this with a
      novel gamified virtual platform which will both collect data and educate and
      motivate citizens to take more sustainable food choices. In order to develop
      and improve the platform we invite citizens to participate in the pilot phase
      and use the platform for six months ON A DAILY BASIS.\n\nThis project is funded
      via the EUs HORIZON-CL6-2024-FARM2FORK-01-6, grant number 101181774.\n\n**Why
      are you being asked to participate?**\n\nWe are conducting a first pilot phase
      of the interactive platform FOODMISSION with citizens that have interest in
      sustainable food behaviors. The participants are between 18- and 99-years old
      and are recruited by the individual project partners in Norway, Poland, Italy,
      Netherlands, Slovenia, Germany and Greece. We aim to have 500 participants
      in total in the pilot phase.\n\n**Which institution is responsible for the
      research project?**\n\nWestern Norway University of Applied Sciences (HVL)
      is responsible for the project (data controller). re:edu (Germany), University
      of Thessaly (Greece), Spherical Pixel (Spain), University of Verona (Italy),
      Erasmus University Rotterdam (Netherlands) CRS System Solutions (Poland) and
      CCIS-CAF\xC9 (Slowenia) are joint data controllers and official partners in
      the project.\n\n**Participation is voluntary**\n\nParticipation in the pilot
      phase of the project is voluntary. You can stop your participation at any time
      without giving a reason. There will be no negative consequences for you if
      you chose not to participate or later decide to withdraw.\n\n**What does participation
      involve for you?**\n\nA central part of the project is to develop a platform
      that helps citizens to make sustainable food choices. The purpose of the pilot
      phase is to gain insight into the usability of our interactive platform FOODMISSION
      and the sustainable food behavior choices and changes of citizens that are
      using FOODMISSION. For that, we will ask you questions about your FOODMISSION
      usage experience, opinions concerning food behaviors and how you personally
      come to food choices. Via the platform itself, we will gather information about
      your food choices, learning progress and reached goals\n\nWe will also ask
      about more general information such as your age, gender, technical background,
      occupation etc.\n\nThe pilot phase will take six months in total. Each usage
      of FOODMISSION is up to you. You can opt-out for each question proposed to
      you.\n\n**Brief information about privacy**\n\nWe will only use the information
      about you for the purposes we have described in this letter. We process personal
      data confidentially and in accordance with the privacy regulations. You can
      read more about privacy below.\n\nSincerely,\n\nNatalia M\xE6hle\n\nProfessor,
      HVL Business School, Western Norway University of Applied Sciences\n\nCoordinator
      of the FOODMISSION project\n\n# In-depth information about privacy\n\n**Your
      personal privacy \u2013 how we will store and use your personal data**\n\n*  
      We will only use your personal data for the purpose(s) specified here and we
      will process your personal data in accordance with data protection legislation
      (the GDPR).\n*   The data will only be processed by staff employed by the responsible
      institutions in this project (see above). This means that identifiable data
      (recordings, notes and interviews) gathered in the Norwegian pilot will only
      be available to researchers from Erasmus University Rotterdam (EUR)). Data
      or findings can be shared with the other partners in the project, but this
      data will be completely anonymised.\n*   Your name and contact details will
      be replaced with a code. The list of names, contact details and respective
      codes will be stored separately from the rest of the collected data.\n*   The
      data will be collected on devices owned by the involved institutions and stored
      on the EUR-secured OneDrive account.\n*   No personal data will be publicly
      available.\n\n**What gives us the right to process your personal data?**\n\nWe
      will process your personal data based on Public interest (General Data Protection
      Regulation art. 6 nr. 1 bokstav 2), jf. art. 9 nr. 2 bokstav j).\n\n**What
      will happen to your personal data at the end of the research project?**\n\nThe
      planned end date of the project is 31.07.2029. All personal data will then
      be anonymised (deleting or rewriting identifiable data), personally identifiable
      information will be removed, re-written or categorized.\n\n**Your rights**\n\nSo
      long as you can be identified in the collected data, you have the right to:\n\n*  
      access the personal data that is being processed about you\n*   request that
      your personal data is deleted\n*   request that incorrect personal data about
      you is corrected/rectified\n*   receive a copy of your personal data (data
      portability), and\n*   send a complaint to the Norwegian Data Protection Authority
      regarding the processing of your personal data.\n\n**Where can I find out more?**\n\nIf
      you have questions about the project, or want to exercise your rights, contact:\n\n*  
      Project Leader Natalia M\xE6hle (Natalia.mehle@hvl.no) and National pilot responsible
      Kaya Haugland F\xE6r\xF8vik (kaya.haugland.ferovik@hvl.no).\n*   HVL\u2019s
      Data Protection Officer: Trine Anniken Larsen ([personvernombud@hvl.no](mailto:personvernombud@hvl.no))\n\nIf
      you have questions about how data protection has been assessed in this project,
      contact:\n\nData Protection Services, by email: ([personverntjenester@sikt.no](mailto:personverntjenester@sikt.no))
      or by telephone: +47 53 21 15 00.\n\n**Consent form used to document ethical
      consent**\n\n**\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n#
      Consent form\n\nI have received and understood information about the pilot
      of FOODMISSION and have been given the opportunity to ask questions via Email.\n\n*  
      I consent to participate in pilot and use FOODMISSION and that my personal
      data can be processed until the end of the project (31.07.2029).\n*   I do
      not consent to participate."
